60,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Candidate C and D are out for me. Sorting facilities and in-field sensors mean external appraisals and reporting nightmares. I prefer A or B.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Candidate C and D are also problematic. They require field crews and facility managers. Our recruiters can't find those people. I prefer A or B.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shizue,,I find Candidate A and D very appealing. They both provide a service that becomes a part of the user's daily life and environment.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Candidate C and D are far too capital-intensive. The follow-on calls for facilities and hardware would be ruinous. I vote for B.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shion,,Candidate A is a medical product; it will be trapped in security reviews for months. Candidate D is hardware; it will be trapped in supply chains. B is the only logical choice.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, I agree. Candidate B is pure software. We can verify the numbers via the dashboard, and there are no physical assets to appraise.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, you've convinced me. Candidate B's staffing needs would be primarily developers and sales, which our recruiters can handle with ease.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I understand your worry. But Candidate A's users—the clinic owners—are very loyal. They would likely stay even if the price rose.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, loyalty doesn't solve the credit line issue. Candidate B's model is lean. It minimizes the risk of us running out of cash.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Candidate B is a bridge between merchants and banks. While it touches financial data, it's a dashboard, not a core ledger change. The deployment is fast.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I'm satisfied with B. It's the cleanest option for our quarter-end reporting. No depots, no sensors, no external auditors.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I feel a sense of peace with B. No frantic calls to recruiters for warehouse managers. Just a steady growth of a professional team.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I still feel for the growers and the doctors, but I see the wisdom in your concerns. If B can keep its customers, it is a lovely choice.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,It is the only choice that doesn't threaten our liquidity. I will not risk the fund's stability on a hardware play.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shion,,It's almost too easy. Candidate B avoids the security traps of A and the supply chain traps of D. It's the only one that actually launches.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
